(19,2,'vulnerability-assessment','Vulnerability Assessment','cyber','Authorised scanning & validation','search','Broad, recurring identification and prioritisation of known vulnerabilities across your estate.','A vulnerability assessment gives you breadth: a systematic inventory of known weaknesses, validated to remove noise and prioritised for remediation.','Vulnerability assessment uses authenticated and unauthenticated scanning, manual validation and risk-based prioritisation (CVSS, exploit availability, asset criticality). Unlike penetration testing, it does not attempt exploitation.','Many frameworks require regular scanning. Consistent, prioritised results let IT teams patch what matters first.',NULL,'Authorisation & scoping :: Signed authorisation, asset list, testing windows, contacts and rules of engagement.\nReconnaissance :: Mapping the authorised attack surface, technologies and entry points.\nAutomated discovery :: Industry-standard scanners to establish baseline coverage.\nManual testing :: Expert-led exploration of business logic, chained weaknesses and false-positive elimination.\nControlled exploitation :: Safe proof-of-concept within agreed limits to demonstrate real impact.\nReporting & retest :: Risk-rated findings, remediation guidance and verification retest.','One-time or recurring (monthly / quarterly) cycles\nInternal and external targets\nAuthenticated scans where possible\nTrend reporting across cycles','Asset discovery & inventory reconciliation\nMissing patches & outdated software\nInsecure configurations\nDefault and weak credentials\nCertificate & TLS issues\nRisk-based prioritisation','Signed scope & rules of engagement\nExecutive and technical VAPT report\nEvidence and proof-of-concept details for each finding\nRemediation tracker (spreadsheet)\nRetest report / closure letter','Executive summary :: Business-level risk overview for leadership.\nTechnical findings :: Each issue with severity (CVSS), affected assets, evidence and reproduction steps.\nRisk heat-map :: Visual distribution of findings by severity and asset.\nWalk-through call :: Findings explained to engineering and management teams.\nRetest letter :: Confirmation of remediated issues after verification.','Prioritised fix list ordered by exploitability and business impact\nDeveloper-friendly guidance with secure configuration and code examples\nCompensating controls where an immediate fix is not feasible\nOptional workshop to address root causes, not just symptoms\nRetest within the agreed window to verify closure','Real-world view of exploitable risk, not just scanner output\nEvidence for ISO 27001, SOC 2, PCI DSS and customer security reviews\nClear priorities for engineering teams\nReduced likelihood and impact of security incidents','Vulnerability Assessment | Yojo Solutions','Broad, recurring identification and prioritisation of known vulnerabilities across your estate.',0,7),
(20,2,'penetration-testing','Penetration Testing','cyber','Authorised adversarial testing','target','Goal-based, manual penetration testing that demonstrates real business impact.','Penetration testing answers the question "what could a determined attacker actually achieve?" by chaining weaknesses towards agreed objectives.','A penetration test is a controlled, authorised simulation of an attack against defined targets. Testers exploit vulnerabilities, misconfigurations and logic flaws to reach objectives such as sensitive data or administrative control, within strict rules of engagement.','Scanner results rarely show impact. Demonstrated attack paths help leadership prioritise investment and satisfy assurance requirements.',NULL,'Authorisation & scoping :: Signed authorisation, asset list, testing windows, contacts and rules of engagement.\nReconnaissance :: Mapping the authorised attack surface, technologies and entry points.\nAutomated discovery :: Industry-standard scanners to establish baseline coverage.\nManual testing :: Expert-led exploration of business logic, chained weaknesses and false-positive elimination.\nControlled exploitation :: Safe proof-of-concept within agreed limits to demonstrate real impact.\nReporting & retest :: Risk-rated findings, remediation guidance and verification retest.','Black, grey or white-box approach\nAgreed objectives ("crown jewels")\nRules of engagement and emergency stop procedure\nOptional purple-team debrief with defenders','Objective-based attack scenarios\nExploitation & chaining of weaknesses\nPrivilege escalation & lateral movement\nDetection & response observation\nData access impact demonstration\nSocial engineering (only when explicitly authorised)','Signed scope & rules of engagement\nExecutive and technical VAPT report\nEvidence and proof-of-concept details for each finding\nRemediation tracker (spreadsheet)\nRetest report / closure letter','Executive summary :: Business-level risk overview for leadership.\nTechnical findings :: Each issue with severity (CVSS), affected assets, evidence and reproduction steps.\nRisk heat-map :: Visual distribution of findings by severity and asset.\nWalk-through call :: Findings explained to engineering and management teams.\nRetest letter :: Confirmation of remediated issues after verification.','Prioritised fix list ordered by exploitability and business impact\nDeveloper-friendly guidance with secure configuration and code examples\nCompensating controls where an immediate fix is not feasible\nOptional workshop to address root causes, not just symptoms\nRetest within the agreed window to verify closure','Real-world view of exploitable risk, not just scanner output\nEvidence for ISO 27001, SOC 2, PCI DSS and customer security reviews\nClear priorities for engineering teams\nReduced likelihood and impact of security incidents','Penetration Testing | Yojo Solutions','Goal-based, manual penetration testing that demonstrates real business impact.',0,8),
(21,2,'configuration-security-assessment','Configuration Security Assessment','cyber','Configuration review','sliders','Benchmark-based review of servers, network devices, databases and SaaS platforms.','Secure configuration is one of the most cost-effective controls available. We compare your settings against recognised hardening baselines.','Configuration security assessment reviews device and system settings against CIS Benchmarks, vendor hardening guides and your own standards, covering firewalls, switches, operating systems, databases, Microsoft 365 / Google Workspace and more.','Default settings favour usability over security. Drift over time silently re-opens risks that were once closed.',NULL,'Authorisation & scoping :: Signed authorisation, asset list, testing windows, contacts and rules of engagement.\nReconnaissance :: Mapping the authorised attack surface, technologies and entry points.\nAutomated discovery :: Industry-standard scanners to establish baseline coverage.\nManual testing :: Expert-led exploration of business logic, chained weaknesses and false-positive elimination.\nControlled exploitation :: Safe proof-of-concept within agreed limits to demonstrate real impact.\nReporting & retest :: Risk-rated findings, remediation guidance and verification retest.','Configuration exports or read-only access\nCIS Benchmark level agreed in advance\nSample of representative systems\nGold-image recommendations','Firewall & router rule-base review\nOS hardening (Windows, Linux)\nDatabase configuration\nMicrosoft 365 / Google Workspace security settings\nLogging & time synchronisation\nBaseline drift','Signed scope & rules of engagement\nExecutive and technical VAPT report\nEvidence and proof-of-concept details for each finding\nRemediation tracker (spreadsheet)\nRetest report / closure letter','Executive summary :: Business-level risk overview for leadership.\nTechnical findings :: Each issue with severity (CVSS), affected assets, evidence and reproduction steps.\nRisk heat-map :: Visual distribution of findings by severity and asset.\nWalk-through call :: Findings explained to engineering and management teams.\nRetest letter :: Confirmation of remediated issues after verification.','Prioritised fix list ordered by exploitability and business impact\nDeveloper-friendly guidance with secure configuration and code examples\nCompensating controls where an immediate fix is not feasible\nOptional workshop to address root causes, not just symptoms\nRetest within the agreed window to verify closure','Real-world view of exploitable risk, not just scanner output\nEvidence for ISO 27001, SOC 2, PCI DSS and customer security reviews\nClear priorities for engineering teams\nReduced likelihood and impact of security incidents','Configuration Security Assessment | Yojo Solutions','Benchmark-based review of servers, network devices, databases and SaaS platforms.',0,9),
(22,2,'secure-code-review','Secure Code Review','cyber','Source code assessment','file-code','Manual and tool-assisted review of source code to find vulnerabilities early in the lifecycle.','Fixing a vulnerability in code review costs far less than fixing it in production. We review high-risk areas of your codebase alongside SAST tooling.','Secure code review examines source code for security flaws such as injection, insecure deserialisation, broken authentication, cryptographic misuse and hard-coded secrets, combining static analysis tools with expert manual review of critical paths.','Code review finds classes of issues that black-box testing cannot reach, and helps engineering teams build secure-coding habits.',NULL,'Authorisation & scoping :: Signed authorisation, asset list, testing windows, contacts and rules of engagement.\nReconnaissance :: Mapping the authorised attack surface, technologies and entry points.\nAutomated discovery :: Industry-standard scanners to establish baseline coverage.\nManual testing :: Expert-led exploration of business logic, chained weaknesses and false-positive elimination.\nControlled exploitation :: Safe proof-of-concept within agreed limits to demonstrate real impact.\nReporting & retest :: Risk-rated findings, remediation guidance and verification retest.','Read-only repository access or code export\nLanguages and frameworks agreed upfront\nRisk-based focus on critical modules\nOptional developer training session','Authentication & authorisation logic\nInput validation & output encoding\nCryptography & secrets management\nError handling & logging\nDependency & supply-chain risk\nFramework-specific security features','Signed scope & rules of engagement\nExecutive and technical VAPT report\nEvidence and proof-of-concept details for each finding\nRemediation tracker (spreadsheet)\nRetest report / closure letter','Executive summary :: Business-level risk overview for leadership.\nTechnical findings :: Each issue with severity (CVSS), affected assets, evidence and reproduction steps.\nRisk heat-map :: Visual distribution of findings by severity and asset.\nWalk-through call :: Findings explained to engineering and management teams.\nRetest letter :: Confirmation of remediated issues after verification.','Prioritised fix list ordered by exploitability and business impact\nDeveloper-friendly guidance with secure configuration and code examples\nCompensating controls where an immediate fix is not feasible\nOptional workshop to address root causes, not just symptoms\nRetest within the agreed window to verify closure','Real-world view of exploitable risk, not just scanner output\nEvidence for ISO 27001, SOC 2, PCI DSS and customer security reviews\nClear priorities for engineering teams\nReduced likelihood and impact of security incidents','Secure Code Review | Yojo Solutions','Manual and tool-assisted review of source code to find vulnerabilities early in the lifecycle.',0,10),
(23,3,'itgc-audit','IT General Controls Audit','it_audit','Independent internal audit','settings','Independent testing of ITGC design and operating effectiveness across in-scope applications.','An ITGC audit gives management and audit committees an independent view of whether the controls underpinning financial systems actually operate.','The audit tests access, change, development and operations controls for applications and supporting infrastructure relevant to financial reporting, using sample-based procedures over a defined period.','Supports Internal Financial Controls attestation, SOX programmes and statutory auditor reliance.','Access provisioning & de-provisioning\nPrivileged access & periodic reviews\nChange authorisation & testing\nBatch job & backup monitoring\nSegregation of duties','Planning & risk assessment :: Understand systems, processes and risks; agree audit objectives and criteria.\nWalkthroughs :: Trace processes end to end with control owners to confirm control design.\nControl testing :: Sample-based testing of operating effectiveness over the audit period.\nEvaluation :: Assess exceptions, root causes and the severity of control deficiencies.\nReporting :: Agree findings with management and capture action plans and owners.\nFollow-up :: Validate that agreed actions have been implemented.','Audit planning memo and risk-and-control matrix (RCM)\nWalkthroughs and design assessment\nOperating-effectiveness testing with documented samples\nManagement responses and action plans\nFollow-up validation of remediation',NULL,'Risk & Control Matrix :: Controls mapped to risks and assertions.\nTest Workpapers :: Documented procedures, samples and results.\nAudit Report :: Rated findings with root cause and recommendations.\nManagement Action Plan :: Owners, due dates and status.',NULL,NULL,'Reliable evidence for statutory auditors and audit committees\nEarly detection of control weaknesses\nReduced reliance on manual, error-prone processes\nStronger governance over technology risk','IT General Controls Audit | Yojo Solutions','Independent testing of ITGC design and operating effectiveness across in-scope applications.',1,1),
(24,3,'itac-audit','IT Application Controls Audit','it_audit','Independent internal audit','grid','Testing of automated controls and system reports within ERP and business applications.','We confirm that automated controls are configured as intended and that key reports are complete and accurate.','Application controls are tested through configuration inspection, re-performance and benchmarking strategies, supported by effective ITGCs.','Validated automated controls reduce manual testing effort and strengthen confidence in financial data.','Configuration inspection\nRe-performance of calculations\nInterface reconciliation\nReport (IPE) validation\nSoD rule testing','Planning & risk assessment :: Understand systems, processes and risks; agree audit objectives and criteria.\nWalkthroughs :: Trace processes end to end with control owners to confirm control design.\nControl testing :: Sample-based testing of operating effectiveness over the audit period.\nEvaluation :: Assess exceptions, root causes and the severity of control deficiencies.\nReporting :: Agree findings with management and capture action plans and owners.\nFollow-up :: Validate that agreed actions have been implemented.','Audit planning memo and risk-and-control matrix (RCM)\nWalkthroughs and design assessment\nOperating-effectiveness testing with documented samples\nManagement responses and action plans\nFollow-up validation of remediation',NULL,'Risk & Control Matrix :: Controls mapped to risks and assertions.\nTest Workpapers :: Documented procedures, samples and results.\nAudit Report :: Rated findings with root cause and recommendations.\nManagement Action Plan :: Owners, due dates and status.',NULL,NULL,'Reliable evidence for statutory auditors and audit committees\nEarly detection of control weaknesses\nReduced reliance on manual, error-prone processes\nStronger governance over technology risk','IT Application Controls Audit | Yojo Solutions','Testing of automated controls and system reports within ERP and business applications.',1,2),
(25,3,'access-management-audit','Access Management Audit','it_audit','Independent internal audit','key','Audit of identity lifecycle, privileged access, MFA and access reviews across critical systems.','Excessive or orphaned access is one of the most common audit findings and breach enablers. We examine how access is granted, reviewed and removed.','The audit covers joiner-mover-leaver processes, role design, privileged accounts, service accounts, multi-factor authentication and the quality of periodic user access reviews.','Strong identity governance limits insider risk, reduces the blast radius of compromised credentials and is central to every security framework.','Joiner / mover / leaver processes\nRole-based access design\nPrivileged & service accounts\nMFA coverage\nUser access review quality','Planning & risk assessment :: Understand systems, processes and risks; agree audit objectives and criteria.\nWalkthroughs :: Trace processes end to end with control owners to confirm control design.\nControl testing :: Sample-based testing of operating effectiveness over the audit period.\nEvaluation :: Assess exceptions, root causes and the severity of control deficiencies.\nReporting :: Agree findings with management and capture action plans and owners.\nFollow-up :: Validate that agreed actions have been implemented.','Audit planning memo and risk-and-control matrix (RCM)\nWalkthroughs and design assessment\nOperating-effectiveness testing with documented samples\nManagement responses and action plans\nFollow-up validation of remediation',NULL,'Risk & Control Matrix :: Controls mapped to risks and assertions.\nTest Workpapers :: Documented procedures, samples and results.\nAudit Report :: Rated findings with root cause and recommendations.\nManagement Action Plan :: Owners, due dates and status.',NULL,NULL,'Reliable evidence for statutory auditors and audit committees\nEarly detection of control weaknesses\nReduced reliance on manual, error-prone processes\nStronger governance over technology risk','Access Management Audit | Yojo Solutions','Audit of identity lifecycle, privileged access, MFA and access reviews across critical systems.',0,3),
(26,3,'change-management-audit','Change Management Audit','it_audit','Independent internal audit','git','Audit of how changes to applications, infrastructure and configurations are authorised, tested and deployed.','Uncontrolled change is a leading cause of outages and integrity issues. We test whether your change process — including CI/CD — enforces the right checks.','The audit reviews change requests, approvals, testing evidence, segregation between development and production, emergency changes and automated pipeline controls.','Demonstrates control over production for auditors and customers while supporting fast, safe delivery.','Change authorisation\nTesting & UAT evidence\nSegregation of duties in deployment\nEmergency change handling\nCI/CD pipeline controls','Planning & risk assessment :: Understand systems, processes and risks; agree audit objectives and criteria.\nWalkthroughs :: Trace processes end to end with control owners to confirm control design.\nControl testing :: Sample-based testing of operating effectiveness over the audit period.\nEvaluation :: Assess exceptions, root causes and the severity of control deficiencies.\nReporting :: Agree findings with management and capture action plans and owners.\nFollow-up :: Validate that agreed actions have been implemented.','Audit planning memo and risk-and-control matrix (RCM)\nWalkthroughs and design assessment\nOperating-effectiveness testing with documented samples\nManagement responses and action plans\nFollow-up validation of remediation',NULL,'Risk & Control Matrix :: Controls mapped to risks and assertions.\nTest Workpapers :: Documented procedures, samples and results.\nAudit Report :: Rated findings with root cause and recommendations.\nManagement Action Plan :: Owners, due dates and status.',NULL,NULL,'Reliable evidence for statutory auditors and audit committees\nEarly detection of control weaknesses\nReduced reliance on manual, error-prone processes\nStronger governance over technology risk','Change Management Audit | Yojo Solutions','Audit of how changes to applications, infrastructure and configurations are authorised, tested and deployed.',0,4),
(27,3,'it-operations-audit','IT Operations Audit','it_audit','Independent internal audit','activity','Review of monitoring, incident, problem, backup and capacity management practices.','Day-to-day IT operations determine reliability. We evaluate whether operational processes are defined, followed and measured.','The audit covers job scheduling, monitoring and alerting, incident and problem management, backup and restore testing, capacity and performance management, and service-level reporting.','Reliable operations protect revenue and customer experience, and reduce the likelihood of data loss.','Monitoring & alerting\nIncident & problem management\nBackup & restore testing\nCapacity management\nSLA reporting','Planning & risk assessment :: Understand systems, processes and risks; agree audit objectives and criteria.\nWalkthroughs :: Trace processes end to end with control owners to confirm control design.\nControl testing :: Sample-based testing of operating effectiveness over the audit period.\nEvaluation :: Assess exceptions, root causes and the severity of control deficiencies.\nReporting :: Agree findings with management and capture action plans and owners.\nFollow-up :: Validate that agreed actions have been implemented.','Audit planning memo and risk-and-control matrix (RCM)\nWalkthroughs and design assessment\nOperating-effectiveness testing with documented samples\nManagement responses and action plans\nFollow-up validation of remediation',NULL,'Risk & Control Matrix :: Controls mapped to risks and assertions.\nTest Workpapers :: Documented procedures, samples and results.\nAudit Report :: Rated findings with root cause and recommendations.\nManagement Action Plan :: Owners, due dates and status.',NULL,NULL,'Reliable evidence for statutory auditors and audit committees\nEarly detection of control weaknesses\nReduced reliance on manual, error-prone processes\nStronger governance over technology risk','IT Operations Audit | Yojo Solutions','Review of monitoring, incident, problem, backup and capacity management practices.',0,5),
(28,3,'cloud-infrastructure-audit','Cloud Infrastructure Audit','it_audit','Independent internal audit','cloud','Governance and control audit of cloud environments, landing zones and shared-responsibility obligations.','Cloud changes how controls are implemented but not the need for them. We audit governance, security and cost controls in your cloud estate.','The audit evaluates cloud governance, account structure, IAM, network design, logging, encryption, change and cost management against your policies and recognised benchmarks.','Provides assurance to leadership and auditors that cloud adoption has not bypassed established controls.','Cloud governance & ownership\nAccount / subscription structure\nIdentity & access\nLogging & monitoring\nCost & resource management','Planning & risk assessment :: Understand systems, processes and risks; agree audit objectives and criteria.\nWalkthroughs :: Trace processes end to end with control owners to confirm control design.\nControl testing :: Sample-based testing of operating effectiveness over the audit period.\nEvaluation :: Assess exceptions, root causes and the severity of control deficiencies.\nReporting :: Agree findings with management and capture action plans and owners.\nFollow-up :: Validate that agreed actions have been implemented.','Audit planning memo and risk-and-control matrix (RCM)\nWalkthroughs and design assessment\nOperating-effectiveness testing with documented samples\nManagement responses and action plans\nFollow-up validation of remediation',NULL,'Risk & Control Matrix :: Controls mapped to risks and assertions.\nTest Workpapers :: Documented procedures, samples and results.\nAudit Report :: Rated findings with root cause and recommendations.\nManagement Action Plan :: Owners, due dates and status.',NULL,NULL,'Reliable evidence for statutory auditors and audit committees\nEarly detection of control weaknesses\nReduced reliance on manual, error-prone processes\nStronger governance over technology risk','Cloud Infrastructure Audit | Yojo Solutions','Governance and control audit of cloud environments, landing zones and shared-responsibility obligations.',0,6),
(29,3,'third-party-risk-assessment','Third-Party Risk Assessment','risk','Assessment · Programme design','users','Assess and monitor security and compliance risks introduced by vendors and service providers.','Your vendors\' weaknesses become your incidents. We assess critical third parties and help you build a sustainable vendor-risk programme.','Third-party risk assessment classifies vendors by criticality, reviews questionnaires and assurance reports (SOC 2, ISO certificates), evaluates contracts and defines monitoring.','Regulators increasingly hold organisations accountable for outsourced activities, and supply-chain attacks continue to rise.','Vendor inventory & tiering\nDue-diligence questionnaires\nAssurance report review\nContractual security clauses\nOngoing monitoring','Planning & risk assessment :: Understand systems, processes and risks; agree audit objectives and criteria.\nWalkthroughs :: Trace processes end to end with control owners to confirm control design.\nControl testing :: Sample-based testing of operating effectiveness over the audit period.\nEvaluation :: Assess exceptions, root causes and the severity of control deficiencies.\nReporting :: Agree findings with management and capture action plans and owners.\nFollow-up :: Validate that agreed actions have been implemented.','Audit planning memo and risk-and-control matrix (RCM)\nWalkthroughs and design assessment\nOperating-effectiveness testing with documented samples\nManagement responses and action plans\nFollow-up validation of remediation',NULL,'Risk & Control Matrix :: Controls mapped to risks and assertions.\nTest Workpapers :: Documented procedures, samples and results.\nAudit Report :: Rated findings with root cause and recommendations.\nManagement Action Plan :: Owners, due dates and status.',NULL,NULL,'Reliable evidence for statutory auditors and audit committees\nEarly detection of control weaknesses\nReduced reliance on manual, error-prone processes\nStronger governance over technology risk','Third-Party Risk Assessment | Yojo Solutions','Assess and monitor security and compliance risks introduced by vendors and service providers.',0,7),
(30,3,'business-continuity-assessment','Business Continuity Assessment','risk','Assessment','refresh','Evaluate continuity and disaster-recovery readiness against business requirements and ISO 22301 good practice.','Plans that are never tested rarely work. We assess whether your continuity and recovery capabilities match what the business actually needs.','The assessment reviews business impact analysis, recovery objectives, DR architecture, plan documentation, exercise history and crisis communication.','Identifies gaps between promised and achievable recovery before a real disruption does.','BIA & recovery objectives\nDR architecture\nPlan documentation\nExercise & test results\nCrisis communication','Planning & risk assessment :: Understand systems, processes and risks; agree audit objectives and criteria.\nWalkthroughs :: Trace processes end to end with control owners to confirm control design.\nControl testing :: Sample-based testing of operating effectiveness over the audit period.\nEvaluation :: Assess exceptions, root causes and the severity of control deficiencies.\nReporting :: Agree findings with management and capture action plans and owners.\nFollow-up :: Validate that agreed actions have been implemented.','Audit planning memo and risk-and-control matrix (RCM)\nWalkthroughs and design assessment\nOperating-effectiveness testing with documented samples\nManagement responses and action plans\nFollow-up validation of remediation',NULL,'Risk & Control Matrix :: Controls mapped to risks and assertions.\nTest Workpapers :: Documented procedures, samples and results.\nAudit Report :: Rated findings with root cause and recommendations.\nManagement Action Plan :: Owners, due dates and status.',NULL,NULL,'Reliable evidence for statutory auditors and audit committees\nEarly detection of control weaknesses\nReduced reliance on manual, error-prone processes\nStronger governance over technology risk','Business Continuity Assessment | Yojo Solutions','Evaluate continuity and disaster-recovery readiness against business requirements and ISO 22301 good practice.',0,8),
(31,4,'enterprise-risk-assessment','Enterprise Risk Assessment','risk','Advisory','chart','Identify, evaluate and prioritise strategic, operational, financial and compliance risks across the organisation.','An enterprise risk assessment gives leadership a single, comparable view of the risks that could prevent the organisation from achieving its objectives.','Aligned to ISO 31000 and COSO ERM principles, the assessment defines risk criteria, facilitates workshops, rates likelihood and impact and links risks to owners and mitigations.','Boards and regulators expect structured risk oversight. A shared risk language improves decision-making and resource allocation.','Risk appetite & criteria\nRisk identification workshops\nLikelihood & impact rating\nRisk ownership\nKey risk indicators','Context & objectives :: Understand business model, obligations, risk appetite and stakeholders.\nDiscovery :: Interviews, document review and data or process mapping.\nAnalysis :: Evaluate risks, gaps and control effectiveness against criteria.\nRecommendations :: Practical, prioritised actions with effort and ownership.\nImplementation support :: Help embed governance, policies and tooling.\nMonitoring :: Define KRIs, review cadence and reporting to leadership.','Stakeholder workshops and interviews\nDocument and process review\nRisk or data mapping\nGap and impact analysis\nRoadmap and governance model',NULL,'Assessment Report :: Findings, ratings and prioritised recommendations.\nRisk / Data Register :: Living register with owners and treatment.\nGovernance Model :: Roles, committees and reporting lines.\nRoadmap :: Phased action plan for leadership approval.',NULL,NULL,'Clear view of the risks that matter most\nDefensible decisions for regulators and customers\nPrivacy and risk built into everyday processes\nBetter allocation of security and compliance budget','Enterprise Risk Assessment | Yojo Solutions','Identify, evaluate and prioritise strategic, operational, financial and compliance risks across the organisation.',1,1),
(32,4,'cyber-risk-assessment','Cyber Risk Assessment','risk','Advisory','shield-alert','Quantify and prioritise cyber risks to critical assets in business terms leadership can act on.','Cyber risk assessment connects threats and vulnerabilities to business impact so security investment can be prioritised rationally.','Using threat scenarios, asset criticality and control effectiveness, we rate cyber risks qualitatively or semi-quantitatively and recommend risk-reducing controls.','Translates technical security into business risk for boards, insurers and regulators.','Crown-jewel asset identification\nThreat scenario modelling\nControl effectiveness review\nRisk rating & heat-map\nTreatment recommendations','Context & objectives :: Understand business model, obligations, risk appetite and stakeholders.\nDiscovery :: Interviews, document review and data or process mapping.\nAnalysis :: Evaluate risks, gaps and control effectiveness against criteria.\nRecommendations :: Practical, prioritised actions with effort and ownership.\nImplementation support :: Help embed governance, policies and tooling.\nMonitoring :: Define KRIs, review cadence and reporting to leadership.','Stakeholder workshops and interviews\nDocument and process review\nRisk or data mapping\nGap and impact analysis\nRoadmap and governance model',NULL,'Assessment Report :: Findings, ratings and prioritised recommendations.\nRisk / Data Register :: Living register with owners and treatment.\nGovernance Model :: Roles, committees and reporting lines.\nRoadmap :: Phased action plan for leadership approval.',NULL,NULL,'Clear view of the risks that matter most\nDefensible decisions for regulators and customers\nPrivacy and risk built into everyday processes\nBetter allocation of security and compliance budget','Cyber Risk Assessment | Yojo Solutions','Quantify and prioritise cyber risks to critical assets in business terms leadership can act on.',1,2),
(33,4,'data-privacy-assessment','Data Privacy Assessment','privacy','Advisory','eye','Assess personal-data practices against DPDPA, GDPR and other applicable privacy requirements.','A privacy assessment maps how personal data flows through your organisation and highlights where practices fall short of legal and customer expectations.','The assessment covers data inventory, lawful basis and consent, notices, rights handling, retention, security, vendor sharing and cross-border transfers.','Privacy expectations are rising across jurisdictions. Understanding your current position is the first step to a credible programme.','Data inventory & mapping\nConsent & notices\nRights handling\nRetention & deletion\nCross-border transfers','Context & objectives :: Understand business model, obligations, risk appetite and stakeholders.\nDiscovery :: Interviews, document review and data or process mapping.\nAnalysis :: Evaluate risks, gaps and control effectiveness against criteria.\nRecommendations :: Practical, prioritised actions with effort and ownership.\nImplementation support :: Help embed governance, policies and tooling.\nMonitoring :: Define KRIs, review cadence and reporting to leadership.','Stakeholder workshops and interviews\nDocument and process review\nRisk or data mapping\nGap and impact analysis\nRoadmap and governance model',NULL,'Assessment Report :: Findings, ratings and prioritised recommendations.\nRisk / Data Register :: Living register with owners and treatment.\nGovernance Model :: Roles, committees and reporting lines.\nRoadmap :: Phased action plan for leadership approval.',NULL,NULL,'Clear view of the risks that matter most\nDefensible decisions for regulators and customers\nPrivacy and risk built into everyday processes\nBetter allocation of security and compliance budget','Data Privacy Assessment | Yojo Solutions','Assess personal-data practices against DPDPA, GDPR and other applicable privacy requirements.',0,3),
(34,4,'privacy-impact-assessment','Privacy Impact Assessment','privacy','Advisory','file-search','Structured DPIA / PIA for new products, systems and high-risk processing activities.','Privacy impact assessments help you identify and minimise privacy risks before launching a product, system or processing activity.','A PIA/DPIA describes the processing, assesses necessity and proportionality, identifies risks to individuals and records the measures adopted to address them.','Required by GDPR for high-risk processing and expected of Significant Data Fiduciaries under the DPDPA; a hallmark of privacy-by-design.','Processing description\nNecessity & proportionality\nRisk identification\nMitigation measures\nSign-off & review','Context & objectives :: Understand business model, obligations, risk appetite and stakeholders.\nDiscovery :: Interviews, document review and data or process mapping.\nAnalysis :: Evaluate risks, gaps and control effectiveness against criteria.\nRecommendations :: Practical, prioritised actions with effort and ownership.\nImplementation support :: Help embed governance, policies and tooling.\nMonitoring :: Define KRIs, review cadence and reporting to leadership.','Stakeholder workshops and interviews\nDocument and process review\nRisk or data mapping\nGap and impact analysis\nRoadmap and governance model',NULL,'Assessment Report :: Findings, ratings and prioritised recommendations.\nRisk / Data Register :: Living register with owners and treatment.\nGovernance Model :: Roles, committees and reporting lines.\nRoadmap :: Phased action plan for leadership approval.',NULL,NULL,'Clear view of the risks that matter most\nDefensible decisions for regulators and customers\nPrivacy and risk built into everyday processes\nBetter allocation of security and compliance budget','Privacy Impact Assessment | Yojo Solutions','Structured DPIA / PIA for new products, systems and high-risk processing activities.',0,4),
(35,4,'data-protection-governance','Data Protection Governance','privacy','Advisory · Programme design','database','Establish roles, policies, committees and metrics that make data protection sustainable.','Privacy programmes fail without clear ownership. We help you design governance that fits your size and regulatory exposure.','Governance design covers privacy leadership roles (including DPO where required), RACI, policies, training, metrics, incident handling and board reporting.','Demonstrates accountability to regulators and gives teams clarity on who decides what.','Roles & RACI\nPrivacy policy framework\nTraining & awareness\nPrivacy KPIs\nBoard reporting','Context & objectives :: Understand business model, obligations, risk appetite and stakeholders.\nDiscovery :: Interviews, document review and data or process mapping.\nAnalysis :: Evaluate risks, gaps and control effectiveness against criteria.\nRecommendations :: Practical, prioritised actions with effort and ownership.\nImplementation support :: Help embed governance, policies and tooling.\nMonitoring :: Define KRIs, review cadence and reporting to leadership.','Stakeholder workshops and interviews\nDocument and process review\nRisk or data mapping\nGap and impact analysis\nRoadmap and governance model',NULL,'Assessment Report :: Findings, ratings and prioritised recommendations.\nRisk / Data Register :: Living register with owners and treatment.\nGovernance Model :: Roles, committees and reporting lines.\nRoadmap :: Phased action plan for leadership approval.',NULL,NULL,'Clear view of the risks that matter most\nDefensible decisions for regulators and customers\nPrivacy and risk built into everyday processes\nBetter allocation of security and compliance budget','Data Protection Governance | Yojo Solutions','Establish roles, policies, committees and metrics that make data protection sustainable.',0,5),
(36,4,'policy-procedure-development','Policy & Procedure Development','advisory','Advisory','file-text','Tailored information security, privacy and IT policies that people can actually follow.','Generic templates rarely survive an audit. We write concise, organisation-specific policies and procedures aligned to your chosen frameworks.','Documentation is mapped to ISO 27001, SOC 2, NIST CSF, DPDPA or GDPR requirements, reviewed with owners and structured for easy maintenance.','Clear policies set expectations, support enforcement and provide auditors with the documented information they require.','Policy hierarchy & ownership\nFramework mapping\nProcedures & work instructions\nVersion control\nApproval & communication','Context & objectives :: Understand business model, obligations, risk appetite and stakeholders.\nDiscovery :: Interviews, document review and data or process mapping.\nAnalysis :: Evaluate risks, gaps and control effectiveness against criteria.\nRecommendations :: Practical, prioritised actions with effort and ownership.\nImplementation support :: Help embed governance, policies and tooling.\nMonitoring :: Define KRIs, review cadence and reporting to leadership.','Stakeholder workshops and interviews\nDocument and process review\nRisk or data mapping\nGap and impact analysis\nRoadmap and governance model',NULL,'Assessment Report :: Findings, ratings and prioritised recommendations.\nRisk / Data Register :: Living register with owners and treatment.\nGovernance Model :: Roles, committees and reporting lines.\nRoadmap :: Phased action plan for leadership approval.',NULL,NULL,'Clear view of the risks that matter most\nDefensible decisions for regulators and customers\nPrivacy and risk built into everyday processes\nBetter allocation of security and compliance budget','Policy & Procedure Development | Yojo Solutions','Tailored information security, privacy and IT policies that people can actually follow.',0,6),
(37,4,'vendor-risk-assessment','Vendor Risk Assessment','risk','Advisory','truck','Point-in-time security and privacy assessment of specific vendors before onboarding or renewal.','Need an independent view of a specific supplier? We assess their security and privacy posture against your requirements.','Includes questionnaire design and analysis, evidence review, interviews and a risk-rated report with recommended contractual and technical safeguards.','Supports informed procurement decisions and regulatory expectations for outsourcing.','Questionnaire design\nEvidence validation\nRisk rating\nContract recommendations\nRemediation follow-up','Context & objectives :: Understand business model, obligations, risk appetite and stakeholders.\nDiscovery :: Interviews, document review and data or process mapping.\nAnalysis :: Evaluate risks, gaps and control effectiveness against criteria.\nRecommendations :: Practical, prioritised actions with effort and ownership.\nImplementation support :: Help embed governance, policies and tooling.\nMonitoring :: Define KRIs, review cadence and reporting to leadership.','Stakeholder workshops and interviews\nDocument and process review\nRisk or data mapping\nGap and impact analysis\nRoadmap and governance model',NULL,'Assessment Report :: Findings, ratings and prioritised recommendations.\nRisk / Data Register :: Living register with owners and treatment.\nGovernance Model :: Roles, committees and reporting lines.\nRoadmap :: Phased action plan for leadership approval.',NULL,NULL,'Clear view of the risks that matter most\nDefensible decisions for regulators and customers\nPrivacy and risk built into everyday processes\nBetter allocation of security and compliance budget','Vendor Risk Assessment | Yojo Solutions','Point-in-time security and privacy assessment of specific vendors before onboarding or renewal.',0,7),
(38,4,'compliance-gap-assessment','Compliance Gap Assessment','advisory','Advisory','checklist','Fast, structured gap analysis against any framework or regulation, with a prioritised roadmap.','Not sure where to start? A compliance gap assessment tells you exactly where you stand and what to do next.','We assess current controls against the chosen standard or regulation, rate each requirement and produce a prioritised, costed roadmap.','A clear baseline enables realistic budgeting and timelines for certification or regulatory deadlines.','Framework selection\nControl-by-control rating\nEvidence sampling\nPrioritised roadmap\nEffort estimation','Context & objectives :: Understand business model, obligations, risk appetite and stakeholders.\nDiscovery :: Interviews, document review and data or process mapping.\nAnalysis :: Evaluate risks, gaps and control effectiveness against criteria.\nRecommendations :: Practical, prioritised actions with effort and ownership.\nImplementation support :: Help embed governance, policies and tooling.\nMonitoring :: Define KRIs, review cadence and reporting to leadership.','Stakeholder workshops and interviews\nDocument and process review\nRisk or data mapping\nGap and impact analysis\nRoadmap and governance model',NULL,'Assessment Report :: Findings, ratings and prioritised recommendations.\nRisk / Data Register :: Living register with owners and treatment.\nGovernance Model :: Roles, committees and reporting lines.\nRoadmap :: Phased action plan for leadership approval.',NULL,NULL,'Clear view of the risks that matter most\nDefensible decisions for regulators and customers\nPrivacy and risk built into everyday processes\nBetter allocation of security and compliance budget','Compliance Gap Assessment | Yojo Solutions','Fast, structured gap analysis against any framework or regulation, with a prioritised roadmap.',0,8);
INSERT INTO `service_faqs` (`service_id`,`question`,`answer`,`sort_order`) VALUES
(1,'Do you issue the certificate or report?','No. We provide consulting, readiness and internal audit services. Certificates and attestation reports are issued by independent accredited bodies or licensed firms that you select. Keeping these roles separate protects the independence of your certification.',1),
(1,'How long does a typical readiness programme take?','It depends on scope, maturity and team availability. A focused gap assessment can take a few weeks, while full implementation for a first-time programme commonly runs several months. We confirm timelines after the scoping workshop.',2),
(1,'Can one programme cover multiple frameworks?','Yes. Many controls overlap (for example ISO 27001, SOC 2 and NIST CSF). We build a unified control set so evidence can be reused across frameworks.',3),
